# NOTE: uses the undirected ha_strong() (zero-arg) for exits to
# exercise that primitive in a demo. A directional variant
# (ha_strong_bullish / ha_strong_bearish) would be a better
# trading choice but is already covered by Strategy 4.
#
# Strategy 6 — Pure HA Pattern Reversal After Streak
#
# Pure Heikin Ashi pattern strategy: enter on a color flip after a
# sustained N+ same-color streak (ha_bullish_reversal /
# ha_bearish_reversal), exit on the FIRST strong HA candle in
# either direction (ha_strong, zero-arg).
#
# Trade-off of the undirected exit: ha_strong() fires on BOTH
# bullish and bearish strong candles. In a LONG position, that
# means a bullish strong candle (which is in our favour) ALSO
# closes the position — an intentionally premature exit when the
# move is still going our way. The same applies symmetrically to
# SHORT positions. The result is a "noisy reversal" strategy that
# exits early on any directional impulse. Sub-optimal for trading
# but the explicit purpose of this demo is coverage of the
# zero-arg ha_strong() primitive in a real strategy — currently it
# only appears in the Tier B feature file.

Feature: Pure HA Pattern Reversal After Streak
  Primary timeframe: 1h
  Parameter streak_length default 3
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 1.5
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 4

  Scenario: Enter long on bullish reversal after bearish streak
    Given no open position
    When ha_bullish_reversal(streak_length)
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long on any strong candle
    Given a long position is open
    When ha_strong()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on bearish reversal after bullish streak
    Given no open position
    When ha_bearish_reversal(streak_length)
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short on any strong candle
    Given a short position is open
    When ha_strong()
    Then short_exit
